  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when you've just installed a new adjustable showerhead and it's not quite working as you'd hoped, right? Before you panic, there are a few simple things you can check yourself. First off, make sure all the connections are snug. Sometimes a loose connection can mess with the water flow and how the spray settings work. Also, double-check that you've used the right sealing method – some models love thread tape, while others are all about those rubber washers, and some just need a good hand-tightening. Skipping this step or using the wrong one can definitely throw things off. If your showerhead has multiple spray patterns, cycle through them all to make sure nothing's jammed. Often, a tiny bit of debris from the old plumbing can get stuck. If you've checked these basic things and it's still not performing, or if you notice any persistent leaks or really low flow, it might be time to bring in a pro. Especially if it's part of a bigger setup with a diverter or backflow prevention, a professional like Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC can quickly diagnose and fix the issue, ensuring everything's working perfectly and up to code.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
